{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Hanging out with Friends"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "That Was a Bagel"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Questions with Sentences / Asking for Clarification"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You ask for clarification when you want more details of what the other person is talking about. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We often ask for clarification when we are not clear on what the other person is referring to. We ask the other person to be more specific by giving more information. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use questions with sentences to ask for clarification. You ask a question including a sentence within the question, like <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think it sounds a bit too intense?</span><br/>Questions with sentences are called <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me ... ?</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Do you know if/which/what ... ?</span> to ask for clarification. <br/>An <span class=\"strong\">embedded question</span> builds on a simple question."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Simple question</span>: Where did you get that bagel? <span class=\"strong\"><br/>Embedded question</span>: Can you tell me where you got that bagel?</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Embedded Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Do you know ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Do you remember ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Can you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Could you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you know what makes Montreal bagels so special?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you tell me where I can find these bagels then?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Perfect vs.The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<ol><li>We use the Present Perfect tense for actions which started in the past and are still happening now OR for finished actions which have a connection to the present.</li><li>We use the Simple Past tense for past events or actions which have no connection to the present.</li></ol>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Rule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect</span> is used when the time period has NOT finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It's the best bagel I've ever had in town.</span> <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Have you tried these bagels?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The time period goes up to the present.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Past</span> is used when the time period HAS finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I had so many bagels the last time I was in New York!</span> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I didn't eat any bagels when I was in New York.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The trip to New York has finished.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bagel"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a round, baked pastry with a hole in the middle"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: New York bagels are my favorite."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use in a conversation about  special food items.  "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nothing comes close"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "nothing else compares to it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Nothing comes close to Montreal bagels."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hands down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without question"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Montreal nightlife beats Boston's hands down."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to dip"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put something down briefly in liquid"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They dip the bagels in honey before they bake them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to boil"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put something in a liquid that has reached boiling temperature (100 degrees Celsius)"}, {"t