 They dip the bagels in honey. Then, they boil them for about two minutes before baking them. That's what gives them their unique texture and flavor.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le01ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "48000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    So Montreal has great jazz and great bakeries. I can't believe I've never been there yet!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>:        Oh, you would love it. They have amazing French bistros, excellent breweries and the nightlife beats Boston's hands down. In my opinion, it's the most fun city I've visited so far.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    Sounds like the perfect weekend getaway with Marco ... Can you tell me where I can find these bagels then?", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le01ob07re2img02.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le01ob07re2img05.jpg"}}], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": []}]}]}